            <ArticleTitle>Acute ST elevation myocardial infarction in early puerperium due to left main coronary thrombosis in a woman with thrombophilic state: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>758-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3283347db9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a middle-aged woman presenting with ST elevation myocardial infarction in early puerperium after Caesarean intervention secondary to left main coronary artery thrombosis, likely to be associated with thrombophilic state and concomitant use of oxytocin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
